; Feature Table
;
; The addresses of the features that the rooms use, which are numbered
; #N$00 to #N$1F. #R$C92C uses the feature numbers of a room to find them. Four
; of the entries are never used, and point at the table itself.
@label=FeatureTable
w$696D DEFW $69AD    ; Feature #N$00: The root door and its frame in the wall at the
                     ; high end of y.
 $696F DEFW $69BE    ; Feature #N$01: The root door and its frame in the wall at the
                     ; high end of x.
 $6971 DEFW $69CF    ; Feature #N$02: The root door and its frame in the wall at the
                     ; low end of y.
 $6973 DEFW $69E0    ; Feature #N$03: The root door and its frame in the wall at the
                     ; low end of x.
 $6975 DEFW $69F1    ; Feature #N$04: The stone door and its frame in the wall at the
                     ; high end of y.
 $6977 DEFW $6A02    ; Feature #N$05: The stone door and its frame in the wall at the
                     ; high end of x.
 $6979 DEFW $6A13    ; Feature #N$06: The stone door and its frame in the wall at the
                     ; low end of y.
 $697B DEFW $6A24    ; Feature #N$07: The stone door and its frame in the wall at the
